sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SCH as Scheduler
    participant CRON as Cron handler
    participant ENG as Engine
    participant ADP as Registry adapter
    participant SYS as System connection
    participant PG as PostgreSQL

    SCH->>CRON: POST with bearer secret
    CRON->>CRON: compare secret, read force flag
    CRON->>ENG: run one round
    ENG->>SYS: read configuration and open queue per salesperson
    SYS->>PG: select
    PG-->>ENG: activity codes, states, floor, ceiling, load

    alt every active salesperson at or above the floor, and not forced
        ENG-->>CRON: nothing to do
        CRON-->>SCH: 200 with no work
    else below the floor
        loop each activity code and state pair, in shuffled order
            ENG->>ADP: search companies
            ADP-->>ENG: rows, or an error recorded for this pair
            ENG->>ENG: normalise, drop known tax IDs, dedupe by company root
        end
        ENG->>ENG: shuffle candidates and assign to the least loaded salesperson
        ENG->>SYS: open transaction
        SYS->>PG: insert batch, upsert companies, insert assignments on conflict do nothing
        PG-->>SYS: inserted and skipped counts
        SYS->>PG: commit
        ENG->>ADP: enrich a bounded batch, free sources, fixed workers
        ADP-->>ENG: company records and officers
        ENG->>SYS: store enrichment results
        ENG->>SYS: write the run record with counts, duration and errors
        ENG-->>CRON: counts per salesperson
        CRON-->>SCH: 200 with the run summary
    end
